cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "dryingfaecal" in publications use:'
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
title: 'dryingfaecal: Experimental Data on Drying of Faecal Sludge and Fresh Faeces'
version: 0.0.0.9000
abstract: Data from the addendum of data related to the drying of faecal sludge from
  on-site sanitation facilities and fresh faeces, published on Gates Open Research
  in 2020 <https://doi.org/10.21955/gatesopenres.1116702.1>. The dataset addendum
  gives an overview of the 137 datasheets of the addendum in eight chapters (thermodynamics,
  kinetics, physicochemical properties, morphological properties, mechanical properties,
  dewatering, disinfection and gas analysis), with the place and the dates of each
  experiment, the description of the feedstock and the link to the file with the raw
  data. The dataset centrifugation holds the results of a dewatering experiment in
  which sludge from an anaerobic baffled reactor, from urine diversion dry toilets
  and from ventilated improved pit latrines, and fresh faeces, were centrifuged, with
  the moisture content and the water activity of the material before and after centrifugation.
